diagnostic_evidence.quote:
$(iii)$ Let $\phi\in\mathcal{M}$, there exists $\sigma$ such that for all $\psi\in\mathcal{B}_{\sigma}(\phi)$, the operator $\nabla^{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathcal{P}} E(\cdot):H_0^1(\mathcal{D})\to H_0^1(\mathcal{D})$ and the functional $\lambda_{(\cdot)}:H^1_0(\mathcal{D})\to \mathbb{R}$ are local Lipschitz continuous at $\phi$, i.e., 
				\begin{align*}
					\big\|\nabla^{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathcal{P}} E(\phi)-\nabla^{\mathcal{R}}_{\mathcal{P}} E(\psi)\big\|_{H^1}\le C_{\phi}\|\phi-\psi\|_{H^1}\quad and\quad \big|\lambda_{\phi}-\lambda_{\psi}\big|\le C_{\phi}\|\phi-\psi\|_{L^p},
				\end{align*}

